Whisper: tracking parameters stripped from a local list only

What: the query stripping list service no longer fetches Mozilla's remote list (Remote
Settings collection "query-stripping"); it uses the local lists only, unless the pref
whisper.cleanlinks.remote_list is set.
Why: Whisper ships its own, longer list in privacy.query_stripping.strip_list
(security/0-whisper-security.js) and keeps the network quiet: the collection has no
copy in the build, so on first use Firefox would download it, and the remote list can
also exempt sites. Copy stripping (the bundled StripOnShare lists) is not affected.
---
diff --git a/toolkit/components/antitracking/URLQueryStrippingListService.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/antitracking/URLQueryStrippingListService.sys.mjs
--- a/toolkit/components/antitracking/URLQueryStrippingListService.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/antitracking/URLQueryStrippingListService.sys.mjs
@@ -179,7 +179,14 @@
 
     // We can only access the remote settings in the parent process. For content
     // processes, we will use sharedData to sync the list to content processes.
-    if (this.isParentProcess) {
+    if (
+      this.isParentProcess &&
+      !Services.prefs.getBoolPref("whisper.cleanlinks.remote_list", false)
+    ) {
+      // Whisper: only the local lists (privacy.query_stripping.strip_list and
+      // allow_list, and the bundled strip-on-share lists); nothing is fetched.
+      this._onRemoteSettingsUpdate([]);
+    } else if (this.isParentProcess) {
       this.#rs = lazy.RemoteSettings(COLLECTION_NAME);
 
       if (!this.#onSyncCallback) {
